Language hooks of a subclass <p>A language library overrides these hooks in a subclass:</p> Hook Kind Description <code>tokenize(text)</code> method Tokenizer when <code>tokenizer</code> is not given; by default a word character <code>\w</code> followed by word characters, combining marks, zero-width joiners and non-joiners and soft hyphens, so that a word in NFD, in Devanagari or in Persian with <code>U+200C</code> stays whole <code>lemmatize(word)</code> method Lemma of a word for <code>use_lexemes=True</code>; the word itself by default <code>number_pattern</code> class attribute Pattern of a number for <code>filter_nums=True</code>, matched against the whole lower-cased word; by default a signed number with separators and an optional percent sign: <code>-5</code>, <code>1990-1995</code>, <code>1,500.50</code>, <code>12/03/2020</code>, <code>3:30</code>, <code>10%</code> <code>messages</code> class attribute Messages of the errors of the parameters, of the text and of the tokenizer; <code>MESSAGES</code> by default CodeResult <pre><code>import re

from anyts import WordsExtractor


class EnglishWords(WordsExtractor):
    number_pattern = re.compile(r"\d+(?:st|nd|rd|th)?")

    def tokenize(self, text):
        return text.split()


EnglishWords(filter_nums=True).extract("The 3rd time")
</code></pre> <pre><code>('The', 'time')
